{"crc":"d1e941f0","kind":"Candidate","payload":{"response":"Looking at the issue, the feature request is to allow `:inherited-members:` option to accept a list of classes (not just a single class or True/None). Currently, the `inherited_members_option` function in `sphinx/ext/autodoc/__init__.py` only returns `'object'` when the option is None or True, or returns the raw argument otherwise.\n\nThe fix needs to:\n1. Update `inherited_members_option` to handle a list of classes\n2. Update the code that uses `inherited-members` to support multiple classes\n\nLet me search for where `inherited-members` is used in the codebase to understand the full impact.\n\nLooking at the code, I can see the `inherited_members_option` function in `sphinx/ext/autodoc/__init__.py`. The issue is that when a list of classes is provided, it should be parsed as a set of class names. Let me also check how this option is used in the ClassDocumenter.\n\nLet me search for the relevant code sections:\n\n# path: sphinx/ext/autodoc/__init__.py\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\ndef inherited_members_option(arg: Any) -> Union[object, Set[str]]:\n    \"\"\"Used to convert the :members: option to auto directives.\"\"\"\n    if arg in (None, True):\n        return 'object'\n    else:\n        return arg\n=======\ndef inherited_members_option(arg: Any) -> Union[object, Set[str]]:\n    \"\"\"Used to convert the :inherited-members: option to auto directives.\"\"\"\n    if arg in (None, True):\n        return {'object'}\n    elif arg:\n        return {x.strip() for x in arg.split(',') if x.strip()}\n    else:\n        return set()\n>>>>>>> REPLACE","round":1,"slot":0},"producer":{"instance":"01KZT124GREW6QHPHT45D7HNDH","kind":"drafter","parent":"01KZT124GJM959P2V3XWMNF3RC"},"schema":"Candidate@1","seq":14,"t":1786506193.138643}
{"crc":"1894e689","kind":"substrate.TriggerFired","payload":{"factory":"validator","firing_key":null,"input_sha256":"sha256:580b931a67a5f3a167104887e3809d2888155dc9e175380320cec82ec3fb3b00","instance":"01KZT12A7JHEVZN5QWRD8BS99C","resolved_input":{"response":"Looking at the issue, the feature request is to allow `:inherited-members:` option to accept a list of classes (not just a single class or True/None). Currently, the `inherited_members_option` function in `sphinx/ext/autodoc/__init__.py` only returns `'object'` when the option is None or True, or returns the raw argument otherwise.\n\nThe fix needs to:\n1. Update `inherited_members_option` to handle a list of classes\n2. Update the code that uses `inherited-members` to support multiple classes\n\nLet me search for where `inherited-members` is used in the codebase to understand the full impact.\n\nLooking at the code, I can see the `inherited_members_option` function in `sphinx/ext/autodoc/__init__.py`. The issue is that when a list of classes is provided, it should be parsed as a set of class names. Let me also check how this option is used in the ClassDocumenter.\n\nLet me search for the relevant code sections:\n\n# path: sphinx/ext/autodoc/__init__.py\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\ndef inherited_members_option(arg: Any) -> Union[object, Set[str]]:\n    \"\"\"Used to convert the :members: option to auto directives.\"\"\"\n    if arg in (None, True):\n        return 'object'\n    else:\n        return arg\n=======\ndef inherited_members_option(arg: Any) -> Union[object, Set[str]]:\n    \"\"\"Used to convert the :inherited-members: option to auto directives.\"\"\"\n    if arg in (None, True):\n        return {'object'}\n    elif arg:\n        return {x.strip() for x in arg.split(',') if x.strip()}\n    else:\n        return set()\n>>>>>>> REPLACE","round":1,"slot":0},"trigger_id":"validate"},"producer":null,"schema":"substrate.TriggerFired@1","seq":15,"t":1786506193.138825}
